Accelerate Your Web Apps with Amazon CloudFront ⚡🚀

Ever wonder how global apps like Netflix or Spotify load instantly, even from different corners of the world?
That’s the magic of a CDN (Content Delivery Network) – and Amazon CloudFront is AWS’s powerful answer to global content delivery!

🔎 What is CloudFront?
Amazon CloudFront is a global content delivery network (CDN) service that:
Caches and serves static & dynamic content from Edge Locations
Reduces latency by bringing content closer to users
Increases availability, performance, and security

🧩 Key Features:
✅ Global Edge Network – 400+ edge locations worldwide
 ✅ HTTPS & SSL support
 ✅ Origin Support – Serve from S3, EC2, ALB, or custom origins
 ✅ Lambda@Edge – Run code at edge locations for customization
 ✅ DDoS Protection – Built-in with AWS Shield

📦 Typical Use Cases:
Website & API acceleration 🌐
Video streaming & media delivery 🎥
Secure content delivery with signed URLs 🔐
Reducing load on backend servers

🧠 CloudFront + S3 Website Hosting:
Host your static website in S3
Add CloudFront in front as a global CDN
Set S3 bucket as the origin
Enable HTTPS using Amazon Certificate Manager (ACM)

📉 Performance Benefit:
Instead of going all the way to your origin server (e.g., S3 in US-East-1), the content is cached in nearby edge locations — reducing latency by up to 60%!

🌐 Bonus: Signed URLs
For paid or private content, use signed URLs and signed cookies to protect access.
